,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExOTg5Mw==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/119893?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kennethreitz","html_url":"https://github.com/kennethreitz","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kennethreitz/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kennethreitz/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kennethreitz/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kennethreitz/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kennethreitz/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kennethreitz/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kennethreitz/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kennethreitz/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kennethreitz/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2012-01-02T03:34:16Z","updated_at":"2012-01-02T03:34:16Z","body":"Correct.\n\nIf someone else can find a heavily maintained and accepted CA bundle (I tried), I'd be happy to use it instead. Mozilla's put a lot of work into that list though, and it's update quite frequently.\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/psf/requests/issues/comments/3327196/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/psf/requests/issues/comments/3327338","html_url":"https://github.com/psf/requests/issues/326#issuecomment-3327338","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/psf/requests/issues/326","id":3327338,"node_id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDMzMjczMzg=","user":{"login":"dropwhile","id":59039,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU5MDM5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/59039?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dropwhile","html_url":"https://github.com/dropwhile","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dropwhile/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dropwhile/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dropwhile/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dropwhile/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dropwhile/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dropwhile/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dropwhile/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dropwhile/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dropwhile/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2012-01-02T04:34:27Z","updated_at":"2012-01-02T04:34:27Z","body":"I don't see how LGPL is incompatible, as use of a cert chain would (in my mind) fall very clearly under use 'as a library' and not be considered a derivative. I am by no means a master of software license law though. \n\nInterestingly, the tornado project includes this file in their package and [repo](https://github.com/facebook/tornado/blob/master/tornado/ca-certificates.crt) (for use in their http_client)  and tornado itself is apache-2.0 licensed.\n","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/psf/requests/issues/comments/3327338/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/psf/requests/issues/comments/3327342","html_url":"https://github.com/psf/requests/issues/326#issuecomment-3327342","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/psf/requests/issues/326","id":3327342,"node_id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDMzMjczNDI=","user":{"login":"kennethreitz","id":119893,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExOTg5Mw==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/119893?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kennethreitz","html_url":"https://github.com/kennethreitz","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kennethreitz/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kennethreitz/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kennethreitz/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kennethreitz/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kennethreitz/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kennethreitz/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kennethreitz/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kennethreitz/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kennethreitz/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2012-01-02T04:36:44Z","updated_at":"2012-01-02T04:38:39Z","body":"Anyone using tornado and packaging that file within their application is now subject to the GPL/MPL.\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/psf/requests/issues/comments/3327342/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/psf/requests/issues/comments/3327434","html_url":"https://github.com/psf/requests/issues/326#issuecomment-3327434","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/psf/requests/issues/326","id":3327434,"node_id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDMzMjc0MzQ=","user":{"login":"dropwhile","id":59039,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU5MDM5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/59039?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dropwhile","html_url":"https://github.com/dropwhile","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dropwhile/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dropwhile/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dropwhile/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dropwhile/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dropwhile/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dropwhile/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dropwhile/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dropwhile/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dropwhile/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2012-01-02T05:03:10Z","updated_at":"2012-01-02T05:08:07Z","body":"As that file is licensed under the gpl _or_ mpl, and reading the actual wording of the licenses, I don't see how that is the case. However, I am not a lawyer, don't deal with license issues often, etc. (some interesting references anyway: [here](http://www.mail-archive.com/modssl-users@modssl.org/msg16980.html), [here](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mozilla_Public_License#Compatibility_with_other_licenses), [here](http://www.mozilla.org/MPL/mpl-faq.html) (see points 6 and 7))\n\nThat said, instead of including the file itself, would it would be enough to document that if you want to use https, you need to configure requests to point at your system ssl ca-certificates bundle? (and/or refer people to the libcurl page showing how to download a version for themselves)? Perhaps with a config.defaults configuration value for the path to the bundle/pem?\n","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/psf/requests/issues/comments/3327434/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/psf/requests/issues/comments/3327468","html_url":"https://github.com/psf/requests/issues/326#issuecomment-3327468","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/psf/requests/issues/326","id":3327468,"node_id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDMzMjc0Njg=","user":{"login":"kennethreitz","id":119893,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExOTg5Mw==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/119893?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kennethreitz","html_url":"https://github.com/kennethreitz","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kennethreitz/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kennethreitz/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kennethreitz/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kennethreitz/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kennethreitz/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kennethreitz/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kennethreitz/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kennethreitz/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kennethreitz/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2012-01-02T05:09:15Z","updated_at":"2012-01-02T05:09:15Z","body":"No, it needs to be 100% completely seamless.\n\nRequests is HTTP for Humans. Not machines.\n\nWeb browsers don't require you to read documentation, download an obscure file, place it in a folder, and configure your system to use it in order to have verified SSL. Neither should your Python HTTP client.\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/psf/requests/issues/comments/3327468/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/psf/requests/issues/comments/3327499","html_url":"https://github.com/psf/requests/issues/326#issuecomment-3327499","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/psf/requests/issues/326","id":3327499,"node_id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDMzMjc0OTk=","user":{"login":"dropwhile","id":59039,"node_id":